    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nCan't copy file into not-yet-existing directory\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. open file explorer\r\n2. yank a file (yy on a file)\r\n3. press p to copy the file into the current dir\r\n4. go to the copy\r\n5. press capital I (insert in front of the filename) and type an arbitrary file path in front that doesn't exist yet\r\n6. attempt to synchronize\r\n7. no new dir and no new file\n\n### Expected behavior\n\na copy of the file is placed in the directory specified, creating any folders needed.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNo file or directories are created",
